[00:14.40]The meditation of my heart,
[00:21.44]The thoughts I ponder through the day—
[00:28.62]May they be pleasing to you, Lord,
[00:35.64]And keep me steadfast in your way.
[00:43.40]When worries weigh upon my mind
[00:50.80]And make me restless in the night,
[00:58.04]Then may I meditate on you
[01:04.21]And things I know to be upright.
[01:16.43]Whatever things are chaste and true,
[01:23.65]Whatever virtue there may be,
[01:30.77]Whatever things well-spoken-of—
[01:37.60]May thoughts of these bring peace to me.
[01:45.42]How precious are your thoughts, O God!
[01:52.39]Beyond all counting is their sum.
[01:59.98]So may I ponder your own words,
[02:06.98]Absorbed in them may I become.
